G3521.b:
⟪νηστεία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< νηστεύω), [in LXX for ⁨צוֹם⁩;] ⟪fasting⟫, ⟪a fast⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of voluntary abstinence from food: ⟦Matthew 17:21|Mt 17:21⟧ (WH, R, txt., om.), ⟦Mark 9:29|Mk 9:29⟧ (WH, txt., R, txt., om.), ⟦Luke 2:37|Lk 2:37⟧, ⟦Acts 14:23|Ac 14:23⟧; of the Day of Atonement, ⟦Acts 27:9|Ac 27:9⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of involuntary abstinence: ⟦2 Corinthians 6:5|II Co 6:5⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 11:27|11:27⟧.†
SYN.: ἀσιτία, q.v.

G3551.b:
⟪νόμος⟫, -ου, ὁ
(< νέμω, to deal out, distribute), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨תּוֹרָה⁩, also for ⁨חֻקָּה⁩, etc.;] that which is assigned, hence, ⟪usage⟫, ⟪custom⟫, then ⟪law⟫; in NT (only in Mt, Jo, Ja, and the Lucan and Pauline bks.);
⟪1.⟫ of law in general: ⟦Romans 3:27|Ro 3:27⟧ ⟦Romans 5:13|5:13b⟧; pl., of divine laws, ⟦Hebrews 8:10|He 8:10⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:16|10:16⟧; ὁ ν. τ. Χριστοῦ, ⟦Galatians 6:2|Ga 6:2⟧; (τ.) ἐλευθερίας, ⟦James 1:25|Ja 1:25⟧ ⟦James 2:12|2:12⟧; βασιλικιός (Hort., in l.; Deiss., LAE, 3673), ⟦James 2:8|Ja 2:8⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of a force or influence impelling to action: ⟦Romans 7:21|Ro 7:21⟧, ⟦Romans 7:23|23a⟧, ⟦Romans 7:25|25⟧ ⟦Romans 8:2|8:2⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Of the Mosaic law: ⟦Matthew 5:18|Mt 5:18⟧, ⟦Luke 2:27|Lk 2:27⟧, ⟦John 1:17|Jo 1:17⟧, ⟦Acts 6:13|Ac 6:13⟧, ⟦Romans 2:15|Ro 2:15⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:8|I Co 9:8⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 1:8|I Ti 1:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:19|He 7:19⟧, al.; ν. Μωυσέως, ⟦Luke 2:22|Lk 2:22⟧, ⟦John 7:23|Jo 7:23⟧, ⟦Acts 15:5|Ac 15:5⟧, al.; κυρίου, ⟦Luke 2:39|Lk 2:39⟧; κατὰ τὸν ν., ⟦Acts 22:12|Ac 22:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:5|He 7:5⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:22|9:22⟧.
⟪4.⟫ Anarthrous (Bl., § 46, 8; ICC on ⟦Romans 2:12|Ro 2:12⟧, ⟦Romans 2:13|13⟧), νόμος,
	⟪(a)⟫ of law in general: ⟦Romans 2:12|Ro 2:12⟧, ⟦Romans 2:14|14b⟧ ⟦Romans 3:20|3:20⟧, ⟦Romans 3:21|21⟧ ⟦Romans 4:15|4:15⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ of the Mosaic law in its quality as law: ⟦Romans 2:14|Ro 2:14a⟧ ⟦Romans 5:20|5:20⟧ ⟦Romans 10:4|10:4⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:19|Ga 2:19⟧, al.; οἱ ἐκ ν., ⟦Romans 4:14|Ro 4:14⟧; ὑπὸ νόμον, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:20|I Co 9:20⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:5|Ga 4:5⟧; ν. πράσσειν (πληροῦν), ⟦Romans 2:25|Ro 2:25⟧ ⟦Romans 13:8|13:8⟧.
⟪5.⟫ Of Christian teaching: ν. πίστεως, ⟦Romans 3:27|Ro 3:27⟧; τ. Χριστοῦ, ⟦Galatians 6:2|Ga 6:2⟧.
⟪6.⟫ By meton., of the books which contain the law;
	⟪(a)⟫ of the Pentateuch: ⟦Matthew 12:5|Mt 12:5⟧, ⟦John 1:45|Jo 1:45⟧, al.; ὁ ν. καὶ οἱ προφῆται, ⟦Matthew 5:17|Mt 5:17⟧, ⟦Luke 16:16|Lk 16:16⟧, al.; ὁ ν. καὶ προφῆται κ. ψαλμοί, ⟦Luke 24:44|Lk 24:44⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of the OT Scriptures in general (as Heb. ⁨תּוֹרָה⁩): ⟦John 10:34|Jo 10:34⟧ ⟦John 12:34|12:34⟧ ⟦John 15:25|15:25⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:21|I Co 14:21⟧, al.

G3565.b:
⟪νύμφη⟫, -ης, ἡ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨כַּלָּה⁩;]
⟪1.⟫ cl., ⟪a bride⟫, ⟪young wife⟫, ⟪young woman⟫: ⟦Matthew 25:1|Mt 25:1⟧, WH, mg., ⟦John 3:29|Jo 3:29⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:23|Re 18:23⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:2|21:2⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:9|9⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:17|22:17⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As freq. in LXX (⟦Genesis 38:11|Ge 38:11⟧, al., for ⁨כַּלָּה⁩;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪bride⟫;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪daughter-in-law⟫) and in MGr. (νύφφη, νύφη), ⟪a daughter-in-law⟫: ⟦Matthew 10:35|Mt 10:35⟧, ⟦Luke 12:53|Lk 12:53⟧.†

G3581.b:
⟪ξένος⟫, -η, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨נׇכְרִי⁩;]
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪foreign⟫, ⟪alien⟫: δαιμόνια, ⟦Acts 17:18|Ac 17:18⟧; διδαχαί, ⟦Hebrews 13:9|He 13:9⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ c. gen. rei, ⟪strange to⟫, ⟪estranged from⟫, ⟪ignorant of⟫: ⟦Ephesians 2:12|Eph 2:12⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪strange⟫, ⟪unusual⟫: ⟦1 Peter 4:12|I Pe 4:12⟧. As subst., ὁ ξ.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a foreigner⟫, ⟪stranger⟫: ⟦Matthew 25:35|Mt 25:35⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:38|38⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:43|43⟧, ⟦Matthew 25:44|44⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:7|27:7⟧, ⟦Acts 17:21|Ac 17:21⟧, ⟦3 John 1:5|III Jo 5⟧; ξένοι κ. τάροικοι (opp. to συμπολῖται, οίκεῖοι), ⟦Ephesians 2:19|Eph 2:19⟧; ξ. καὶ παρεπίδημοι, ⟦Hebrews 11:13|He 11:13⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ one of the parties bound by ties of hospitality;
	⟪α⟫ ⟪the guest⟫;
	⟪β⟫ ⟪the host⟫ ( = ξενοδόκος, Hom., Il., xv, 532): ⟦Romans 16:23|Ro 16:23⟧.†
